dist/
build/

# Local-only project direction — not published to the remote
roadmap-fliphex-v1.md

# Local-only tooling config — never published
.claude/

# Example source artifact (USP poster) — local only
FLIPHEX.pdf

# Large artifacts — tracked selectively, see docs/engineering.md
data/models/*.pt
data/selfplay/
# Crash-resume layers (solver/checkpoint.py). ~4.4 GB for one 5×3 arm, and
# reproducible from the run itself — the JSON artefact is the deliverable.
data/checkpoints/
results/*.jsonl
# EXP-006's agreement rows are the exception: which move each champion chose on
# each position, and whether it kept the win. The JSON artefact holds only the
# per-k aggregates, so without this the depth gradient can be quoted but never
# re-derived, and "which positions did all five get wrong" is unanswerable.
!results/exp006-agreement-5x5.jsonl
# The ground-truth work file is *not* an exception: exp006_ground_truth.py
# embeds all 750 position records in its JSON artefact, so tracking the JSONL
# would store the same rows twice.
data/ground-truth/*.jsonl
#
# The rule the two EXP-006 decisions imply, written down so the next one is not
# a coin flip: **track the per-item record when regenerating it needs something
# the repository does not have.** EXP-006's agreement rows need the five
# EXP-015 champions, which are gitignored run directories costing 27 h each, so
# they are tracked. EXP-017's 5,000 game records are 5.1 MB of move strings that
# a tracked, deterministic, single-process instrument regenerates from one seed
# in three hours, and its JSON artefact already carries every aggregate the
# analysis reads — so they are not. Reproducibility is the test, not size.
figures/*.png
!figures/.gitkeep
notes/sources/
refs/
data/az-runs/

# Node, for web/ tests only. The page itself needs no build step.
web/node_modules/
web/package-lock.json
